From d23ca354cf524a4ac683f5d5c9e8df1bbc6b4926 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 14:01:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] avcodec/ppc: restore AltiVec lossless_audiodsp
 scalarproduct_and_madd_int16

Upstream removed libavcodec/ppc/lossless_audiodsp_altivec.c in 35464ad9ebe1
("remove broken AltiVec acceleration for lossless audio"): it failed
checkasm sporadically and tripped the UB/address sanitizers. That predates
the 9.0 branch, so this 9.0.2 base has no PPC acceleration for the APE and
16-bit WMA Lossless inner filter loop at all -- both run the scalar C
scalarproduct_and_madd_int16 on G4/G5.

Restore the kernel with the three defects of the original fixed, so it is
now bit-exact against the C reference:

1. Saturating reduction. The original combined the four int32 lanes with
   vec_sums (vsumsws), which saturates, while the C reference accumulates an
   unsigned that wraps mod 2^32. checkasm feeds 1088 full-range int16
   products, so the lane sums overflow int32 and the saturating combine
   diverged from C for a seed-dependent fraction of runs -- the reported
   "fails sporadically", and endian-independent. Reduced here with modular
   vec_add + vec_sld rotates.

2. Out-of-bounds read. The big-endian load prefetched two aligned quadwords
   ahead (vec_ld(32, src)) and so read a full 16-byte block past the end of
   v2/v3 on the final iteration -- the sanitizer trigger. Each 16-int16
   window is now read with the standard unaligned_load splice, which never
   reads beyond the aligned block holding the window's last byte.

3. Shared alignment permute. A single vec_lvsl derived from v2 was reused to
   align v3. WMA Lossless passes prevvalues+recent and lms_updates+recent
   from two independent arrays whose residues differ, so this was wrong for
   that caller (APE happens to keep them congruent); unaligned_load
   recomputes the permute per source.

v1 stays on aligned loads/stores (16-aligned by contract in APE, WMALL and
checkasm). order is a multiple of 16 for every real caller (APE orders
16/32/64/256/1280, WMALL FFALIGN(order,16)) and checkasm (1088), matching
the header contract. The int32 variant (24-bit WMA Lossless) needs a
32x32->64 widening MAC that classic AltiVec lacks and is left on C.

Numerics verified bit-exact against the C reference (return value and the
in-place v1 update) over 200000 randomized cases spanning all real orders
and full-range int16, including the inputs that made the original saturate.
Intrinsic use syntax-checked with the powerpc-linux-gnu-gcc-14 cross
compiler (-maltivec, -Wall -Wextra, clean). NOT yet run under the qemu
checkasm harness (oracle: checkasm llauddsp, scalarproduct_and_madd_int16)
-- the S1 build dir needs rebuilding first.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 libavcodec/lossless_audiodsp.c             |   2 +
 libavcodec/lossless_audiodsp.h             |   1 +
 libavcodec/ppc/Makefile                    |   1 +
 libavcodec/ppc/lossless_audiodsp_altivec.c | 120 +++++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 124 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 libavcodec/ppc/lossless_audiodsp_altivec.c

diff --git a/libavcodec/lossless_audiodsp.c b/libavcodec/lossless_audiodsp.c
index 2d57857dad..43733d8cb6 100644
--- a/libavcodec/lossless_audiodsp.c
+++ b/libavcodec/lossless_audiodsp.c
@@ -61,6 +61,8 @@ av_cold void ff_llauddsp_init(LLAudDSPContext *c)
 
 #if ARCH_ARM
     ff_llauddsp_init_arm(c);
+#elif ARCH_PPC
+    ff_llauddsp_init_ppc(c);
 #elif ARCH_RISCV
     ff_llauddsp_init_riscv(c);
 #elif ARCH_X86 && HAVE_X86ASM
diff --git a/libavcodec/lossless_audiodsp.h b/libavcodec/lossless_audiodsp.h
index e89e27fef0..cf2d43d7c9 100644
--- a/libavcodec/lossless_audiodsp.h
+++ b/libavcodec/lossless_audiodsp.h
@@ -45,6 +45,7 @@ typedef struct LLAudDSPContext {
 
 void ff_llauddsp_init(LLAudDSPContext *c);
 void ff_llauddsp_init_arm(LLAudDSPContext *c);
+void ff_llauddsp_init_ppc(LLAudDSPContext *c);
 void ff_llauddsp_init_riscv(LLAudDSPContext *c);
 void ff_llauddsp_init_x86(LLAudDSPContext *c);
 
diff --git a/libavcodec/ppc/Makefile b/libavcodec/ppc/Makefile
index 63ece26259..e8d8c00b5a 100644
--- a/libavcodec/ppc/Makefile
+++ b/libavcodec/ppc/Makefile
@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@ OBJS-$(CONFIG_VP8DSP)                  += ppc/vp8dsp_altivec.o
 # decoders/encoders
 OBJS-$(CONFIG_AAC_DECODER)            += ppc/sbrdsp.o ppc/aacpsdsp.o
 OBJS-$(CONFIG_HEVC_DECODER)            += ppc/hevcdsp.o
+OBJS-$(CONFIG_LLAUDDSP)                += ppc/lossless_audiodsp_altivec.o
 OBJS-$(CONFIG_MPEG4_DECODER)           += ppc/mpeg4videodsp.o
 OBJS-$(CONFIG_OPUS_DECODER)            += ppc/opusdsp_altivec.o
 OBJS-$(CONFIG_SVQ1_ENCODER)            += ppc/svq1enc_altivec.o
diff --git a/libavcodec/ppc/lossless_audiodsp_altivec.c b/libavcodec/ppc/lossless_audiodsp_altivec.c
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..95bbdaa596
--- /dev/null
+++ b/libavcodec/ppc/lossless_audiodsp_altivec.c
@@ -0,0 +1,120 @@
+/*
